{"question_id": "V2-dev-BOOK-en-T2-002", "approach": "HYBRID", "approach_base": "HYBRID", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "K", "corpus_set": "BOOK_en", "answer_text": "Douglass first learned from Mrs. Auld, his master's wife, who kindly began teaching him the A, B, C and then helped him spell words of three or four letters (Chapter VI). Mr. Auld found out and forbade her to continue, saying it was unlawful and unsafe to teach a slave to read, that learning would spoil a slave and forever unfit him to be a slave, and that \"if you give a nigger an inch, he will take an ell\" (Chapter VI). Douglass nevertheless finished learning to read and write in Baltimore with the assistance of his master's wife (biographical note).", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 997 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::o011", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b109", "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b110"], "kind": "chunk", "score": 0.032522, "rank": 0, "span": [76333, 77330], "meta": {"chunk": 5734, "mode": "window", "partial_unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b109", "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b110"], "ranks": {"bm25": 1, "dense": 2}, "scores": {"bm25": 15.107973, "dense": 0.629663}, "rrf": 0.032522}}, {"text": "[stripped: 611 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en", "section_id": "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::o015", "unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b197", "K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b198"], "kind": "chunk", "score": 0.032266, "rank": 1, "span": [173632, 174243], "meta": {"chunk": 5877, "mode": "window", "partial_unit_ids": ["K.gutenberg-23_douglass_narrative.en::p1_b197"], "ranks": {"bm25": 3, "dense": 1}, "scores": {"bm25": 11.882374, "dense": 0.632948}, "rrf": 0.032266}}, {"text": "[stripped: 886 chars]", "doc_id": "K.gut